@startuml
title Combined Firebase Authentication Flows

' Define participants
participant User
participant Frontend as App
participant "Firebase Auth" as FA
participant Backend
database Database as DB
participant "Social Provider (e.g., Google)" as SP

' Optional: Set a global layout direction if desired
' left to right direction

== Email/Password Registration ==

User -> App +: User fills registration form
return Submits email, password
App -> FA +: createUserWithEmailAndPassword(email, password)
return Success/Failure Response (User object)


alt Registration Success
  App -> App : User created in Firebase, emailVerified: false
  note over App: Optionally show "Verify Email" prompt
  App -> FA +: sendEmailVerification()
    FA -> FA: Generate verification link
    FA --> User: Send verification email with link
  return Success/Failure Response

  ' Integrate with your backend/database after successful Auth registration
  App -> Backend: POST /api/users (Firebase User UID, email, etc.)
  activate Backend
  note left of Backend: Verify Firebase ID Token (optional but good practice)
  Backend -> DB: Create new user profile/record
  activate DB
  DB --> Backend: Confirmation
  deactivate DB
  Backend --> App: User profile created response
  deactivate Backend

else Registration Failure (e.g., email exists, weak password)
  App -> App: Display error message to user
end

== Email/Password Login ==

App -> User: User fills login form
User -> App: Submits email, password
App -> FA: signInWithEmailAndPassword(email, password)
activate FA
FA --> App: Success/Failure Response (User object, ID Token)
deactivate FA

alt Login Success
  App -> App: User logged in (session managed by Firebase SDK)
  note over App: Check user.emailVerified status
  App -> Backend: GET /api/profile (Include Firebase ID Token in Authorization header)
  activate Backend
  Backend -> FA: Verify ID Token (using Firebase Admin SDK)
  activate FA
  FA --> Backend: User UID from token
  deactivate FA
  Backend -> DB: Fetch user profile data using UID
  activate DB
  DB --> Backend: User profile data
  deactivate DB
  Backend --> App: User profile data
  deactivate Backend
  App -> App: Display application content based on profile & verification status

else Login Failure (e.g., incorrect credentials)
  App -> App: Display error message to user
end

== Logout ==

App -> User: Clicks Logout button
App -> FA: signOut()
activate FA
FA -> App: Clear authentication state (tokens, session)
FA --> App: Success Response
deactivate FA

App -> App: Clear local user data/state
App -> App: Redirect to public page (e.g., login or homepage)

== Password Reset Request ==

App -> User: User clicks "Forgot Password"
User -> App: Enters email address
App -> FA: sendPasswordResetEmail(email)
activate FA
FA -> FA: Check if email exists in Firebase Auth
FA -> User: Send password reset email with link (if email exists)
FA --> App: Success/Failure Response
deactivate FA

App -> User: Instructs user to check email

== Password Reset Confirmation ==

User -> App: Clicks password reset link in email (Navigates to your app with oobCode)
App -> App: Extract oobCode from URL
App -> FA: verifyPasswordResetCode(oobCode) ' Optional: Check code validity and get email
activate FA
FA --> App: User email / Error
deactivate FA

alt Code is valid
  App -> App: Display form to set new password
  User -> App: Enters and submits new password
  App -> FA: confirmPasswordReset(oobCode, newPassword)
  activate FA
  FA -> FA: Verify oobCode again, update user password
  FA -> FA: Invalidate oobCode
  FA --> App: Success/Failure Response
  deactivate FA
  App -> App: Inform user password reset is complete
  App -> App: Suggest logging in with new password

else Code is invalid or expired
  App -> App: Display error message (e.g., "Invalid or expired reset link")
end

== Email Verification Confirmation ==

User -> App: Clicks email verification link (Navigates to your app with oobCode and mode=verifyEmail)
App -> App: Extract oobCode from URL
App -> FA: applyActionCode(oobCode)
activate FA
FA -> FA: Verify oobCode, mark user's email as verified
FA -> FA: Invalidate oobCode
FA --> App: Success/Failure Response
deactivate FA

alt Verification Success
  App -> FA: user.reload() ' Get updated user state
  activate FA
  FA --> App: Updated User object (emailVerified: true)
  deactivate FA
  App -> App: Update UI / Grant full access
  App -> App: Inform user email is verified
  App -> App: Redirect to relevant page
else Verification Failure (e.g., invalid or expired code)
  App -> App: Display error message
  App -> App: Maybe provide option to resend verification email
end

== Social Login (High-Level via Popup/Redirect) ==

App -> User: Clicks "Sign in with Social Provider" button
App -> FA: signInWithPopup() or signInWithRedirect()
activate FA
FA -> SP: Initiate OAuth flow (Redirect/Popup)
activate SP
User -> SP: Authenticates with Social Provider
SP --> FA: Authorization code/token
deactivate SP
FA -> SP: Exchange code/token for user info (Server-to-server)
activate SP
deactivate SP
FA -> FA: Create or link Firebase user account
FA -> FA: Issue Firebase ID Token
FA --> App: Success/Failure Response (User object, ID Token)
deactivate FA

alt Login Success
  App -> App: User logged in with social account
  App -> Backend: GET /api/profile (Include Firebase ID Token in Authorization header)
  activate Backend
  Backend -> FA: Verify ID Token (using Firebase Admin SDK)
  activate FA
  FA --> Backend: User UID from token
  deactivate FA
  Backend -> DB: Fetch or create user profile data using UID
  activate DB
  DB --> Backend: User profile data
  deactivate DB
  Backend --> App: User profile data
  deactivate Backend
  App -> App: Display application content

else Login Failure (e.g., user cancels)
  App -> App: Display error message or return to previous state
end

@enduml